Z||000000||KnightRyder31||09-15-2000||10:09 AM||||Anyone here know how to make a custom air intake? I was thinking about doing one, but I really don't know where to start. Isn't there an air restricter on the intake already? I wonder where that is? And if I did make a custom intake, how much power could I get?||||reg||1
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||09-15-2000||11:02 AM||||I've done some preliminary designs for a ram air intake, with part of it based on the intake from an SR-71 Blackbird...<P>email me if you're interested in discussing this project!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000002||fotofrank||09-15-2000||12:54 PM||||When you say air intake are you talking about "Ram Air" or an intake "manafold"? if it is a manafold you would be better off adding a spacer (about 1/2 to 3/4 inch thick) for the 2.5L. For the V6 good luck. If the runners are equal in length and a bit longer than stock low end power incresses (hence the spacer on an Iron Duke) <P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://fotofrank.homestead.com/foto1~ns4.html||||reg||11
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||09-15-2000||03:23 PM||||hmm.. somehow I managed a double post, but 4 hours apart......<p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 09-15-2000).]||||reg||3
Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||09-15-2000||05:19 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fotofrank:<BR><B>When you say air intake are you talking about "Ram Air" or an intake "manafold"? if it is a manafold you would be better off adding a spacer (about 1/2 to 3/4 inch thick) for the 2.5L. For the V6 good luck. If the runners are equal in length and a bit longer than stock low end power incresses (hence the spacer on an Iron Duke) <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>a longer intake manifold increases low end power? I was planning to get a bored out TB/intake, but I hadn't heard anything about a longer manifold.. can anyone explain this?<P>thanks!<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||5
Z||000005||Phil||09-15-2000||05:23 PM||||Read on some web page that actual flow tests(with instruments and all) showed that the stock Fiero air intake system is quite efficent and does not leave much room for improvement.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fotofrank||09-15-2000||05:34 PM||||I'm refering to the runners of the intake manafold. The relationship between the length of the runner and the diameter of the narrowest part of the runners effects power(read torque). Can I explane it ...NO. <BR>If you dobt me, than why do companies like Holley sell spacers for TBI and carberators?<BR>The Holley performance intake ,for the Iron Duke, has longer runners that appear to have the same distance from the TB to each cylender and also a deeper plenum(?). The so called restrictor plate in the stock Iron Duke helps destribute the gas/air mixture evenly to each cylander. As you mat note the restrictor is between the TB and the two center cylanders. This keeps the center two from recieving to much go juce and the two end (1&4) cylanders from recieving too little. With out the restrictor the car may seem faster but effecancy and other factors are effected. Think about running on 3 cylanders and how the car accelerates? That A$$ o'meter can tell a lot.  Hope this helps. <P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://fotofrank.homestead.com/foto1~ns4.html||||reg||3
Z||000007||Loki||09-15-2000||08:05 PM||||Well here is a new intake on the market...which I want...<BR> <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com/Intake/Intake.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cwestco.com/Intake/Intake.html</A> <P>The top one of course<P>Loki||||reg||1
Z||000008||KnightRyder31||09-16-2000||11:30 AM||||Isn't there an air restricter that you can remove? Also, how much HP would the performence plugs and wires...with coil, add on my car? Is it a good idea? Darklord, if that project wont kill my car, or isn't to expensive, sure...I'll give it a shot.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Standard||09-16-2000||11:42 AM||||The stock v6 intake manifold already has long, equal length runners to increase low-end torque.  <BR>let me edit that... long equal length tuned runners to produce the maximum torque at 3600 RPM.  <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/v6_intake_design.jpg">  <BR>check out <A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/wpfc/MT2.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nbci.com/wpfc/MT2.html</A> <P>That "restrictor" in the v6 air intake is a water seperator/silencer.  That little hole at the bottom that you see after you remove the grill is just to let water drain out, not to let air in.  Air actually goes up over the top of that plate.  No real benefits or disadvantages to removing it, unless you drive in a monsoon all the time.<P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 150,000 miles and counting!        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">     <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker<p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 09-16-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||DaRkLoRD||09-16-2000||01:05 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KnightRyder31:<BR><B>Darklord, if that project wont kill my car, or isn't to expensive, sure...I'll give it a shot.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The most expensive part would be an air filter for it, I plan on using a K&N cone filter. The rest is just flex tube and molded plastic.. as for the possibility of killing your car... it works basically the same as the one Loki posted, except the filter end is different.. I think the only danger this would have possibly is heat from the engine melting the intake hose connecting the ram air to the TB.. however, the Fiero engine already has a plastic intake, and I've never heard of any problems with that...<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
