Z||000017||DaRkLoRD||09-17-2000||12:36 PM||||That's correct.. an intake like the one Loki posted wouldn't be much more efficient, but it would sound different..<P>mine is a ducted intake.. not open to the engine bay. all of the air that enters the scoop goes into the engine.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000018||DaRkLoRD||09-17-2000||12:53 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 2xsess:<BR><B>Darklord, How much do you think your idea would cost to produce?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'm not sure.. probably at least $100, including the air filter..<BR>that's for the production version.. the prototype will cost $100-$200 most likely, including labor, parts, etc. All it is right now is an idea.. nowhere close to being ready for sale. I'm pretty sure it will allow some improvement over the stock intake, but I could be wrong.. I won't know until I build a prototype and do some tests with it.<P>and if it turns out to not work well for the Fiero... I'll be a bit embarrased.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>I hope people here wouldn't be too mad if I wasn't able to pull this off...<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000019||pHoOl||09-17-2000||03:53 PM||||Can anybody explain exactly what a "ram air" feature is?  I mean, i know it looks cool to have the words, RAM AIR on your Trans Am, but besides that, what does it do?  <P>Here is what i think that it does and somebody let me know if i'm right, close, or way off:<P>  As the car drives (forward) there is air flowing all around the car.  So the ram air, takes the air in such that it comes in at high velocity.  My guess is that at this point, since it can't flow as fast as it's coming in, it starts to get pressurized, like a turbo intake, except probably not as much.<P><BR>That's my guess.  Somebody smack me if i'm wrong or something.<P><BR>Darklord, do you need anybody else to test this?  i wouldn't mind trying to build myself one and try it out.  <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
